# INT-463, INT-467 — the one resource ceiling for every runner of the
# intake-aws-ci pool and its rootless Docker daemon: the pool shares it, so
# adding a runner never takes more from staging than one runner could. The host
# also serves synthetic staging, so CI gets a quarter of the default CPU and IO
# weight, at most seven of the eight cores, and a hard memory ceiling. The job and
# Docker units also set OOMScoreAdjust=500, so under memory pressure the kernel
# kills CI before staging.
#
# INT-544: read on 16 Oct 2026 at 17:12Z (8 vCPU, CPU pressure avg60 0.05,
# 30 GiB RAM with 25 GiB available), the slice's memory peak was 15.0 GB with
# three runners, at its MemoryHigh of 14G (15.03 GB): the pool was already
# being throttled. For five runners the ceiling rises to MemoryHigh 20G and
# MemoryMax 22G, which leaves staging about 8 GiB, and to 700 % CPU.
[Unit]
Description=Resource ceiling for the intake-aws-ci Actions runner pool (INT-463, INT-467)
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
CPUWeight=25
CPUQuota=700%
IOWeight=25
MemoryHigh=20G
MemoryMax=22G
TasksMax=16384
